mn27:15.4 starts: On smelling an odour with the nose…
mn27:15.5 starts: On tasting a flavour with the tongue…
mn27:15.6 starts: On touching a tangible with the body…
mn27:15.7 starts: On cognizing a mind-object with the mind,
mn27:25.2 starts: He understands as it actually is:
mn27:25.3 starts: ‘These are the taints’;…‘This is the origin
sn35.93:1.2 starts: And how, bhikkhus, does consciousness come to be
